{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBUqNzyBxCi1rd5tZUKA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted index 14 (Co 0.51 / Sb 0.49) as the best composition. It had the highest efficiency (EQE) of the three samples I could measure, at 0.024%, but I only tested 3 of the 30 compositions, so the true best may lie elsewhere.\n\n| Index | Co / Sb | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 19 | 0.34 / 0.66 | 0.0124 |\n| **14** | **0.51 / 0.49** | **0.0240** |\n| 9 | 0.67 / 0.33 | 0.0018 |\n\n- **Why I started at index 19:** its 1:2 Co:Sb ratio matches CoSb₂O₆, a compound already known to work as a photoanode.\n- **What the numbers show:** efficiency roughly doubled going from index 19 to the 50:50 composition, then fell by a factor of about 13 at the Co-rich end. The peak is probably somewhere around Sb 0.45–0.6.\n- **Main gap:** with three points, the best composition could be an unmeasured neighbour such as index 13 or 15–17, and the score only counts compositions actually measured.\n- **Not used:** I didn't use any of the 5 XRD scans. They would have shown the crystal structure but can't add efficiency measurements."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":402,"cache_read_input_tokens":7969,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":402},"output_tokens":434,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a3776961-c4ad-4384-b0e0-8dd02e3cfa3f","uuid":"40836b73-f0e5-4358-a220-78f2731242f7","timestamp":"2026-09-18T19:46:27.828Z","request_id":"req_011CfBUqNXhFT6u84eRVUme9"}
